Short:        Small web browser for AmigaOS 3.2 (no WebKit)
Author:       AmigaChrome Team
Uploader:     UPLOADER-PLACEHOLDER
Type:         comm/www
Version:      0.4.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Distribution: Aminet

OpenBrowser Lite is a small web browser for AmigaOS 3.2: a GadTools window
that opens http:// and https:// pages and lays them out, in about 100 KB.

What it shows:
  - headings, paragraphs, lists, quotes, preformatted text, rules
  - links: click one to follow it, or pick it from Links...
  - pictures, through the system's datatypes (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP and
    more, whichever datatypes are installed), scaled to their box
  - CSS: the page's <style>, style= and up to eight linked stylesheets;
    element, class and ID selectors; colours, sizes, margins, padding,
    alignment, display: none
  - Back, Reload, an address field, and ARexx: OPENURL <address> on the
    port AMIGACHROME.BROWSER (OpenMail opens its links that way)

What it doesn't do: JavaScript, forms, frames, table grids, web fonts. For
those there is OpenBrowser on WebKit (much larger).

Requirements:
  - AmigaOS 3.2 or newer
  - a 68040 with FPU (hard float; not an LC or EC040)
  - a TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library)
  - for https://: OpenTLS (LIBS:opentls.library and opencrypto.library) and
    its CA list, S:OpenTLS/ca-bundle.pem (OpenUp's OpenTLS part)

Its page engine, weblayout, is built on OpenLayout and kept behind one
header so that it can become a shared weblayout.library.

